INSERT INTO sentences (id,paper_id,paragraph_index,sentence_index,source_text,section_id) VALUES ('cet4-2024-06-1-section-4-sentence-6-1','cet4-2024-06-1',305,0,'If we base our worth on the opinions of others, we cheat ourselves of the power to shape our experiences and embrace life not only for others but also for ourselves, because ultimately, there is no difference.','cet4-2024-06-1-section-4') ON CONFLICT (id) DO UPDATE SET paragraph_index=EXCLUDED.paragraph_index,sentence_index=EXCLUDED.sentence_index,source_text=EXCLUDED.source_text,section_id=EXCLUDED.section_id;
INSERT INTO sentences (id,paper_id,paragraph_index,sentence_index,source_text,section_id) VALUES ('cet4-2024-06-1-section-4-sentence-6-2','cet4-2024-06-1',305,1,'So embrace the cliché (老话) and love yourself as it''s highly doubtful that you''ll regret it.','cet4-2024-06-1-section-4') ON CONFLICT (id) DO UPDATE SET paragraph_index=EXCLUDED.paragraph_index,sentence_index=EXCLUDED.sentence_index,source_text=EXCLUDED.source_text,section_id=EXCLUDED.section_id;
INSERT INTO paper_sections (id,paper_id,position,kind,title,instructions,paragraphs_json,study_paragraphs_json) VALUES ('cet4-2024-06-1-section-5','cet4-2024-06-1',4,'reading','仔细阅读 · Passage Two（51–55）','There are 2 passages in this section. Each passage is followed by some questions or unfinished statements. For each of them there are four choices marked A), B), C) and D). You should decide on the best choice and mark the corresponding letter on Answer Sheet 2 with a single line through the centre.','["Some people have said aging is more a slide into forgetfulness than a journey towards wisdom. However, a growing body of research suggests that late-in-life learning is possible. In reality, education does an aging brain good.","Throughout life, people''s brains constantly renovate themselves. In the late 1960s, British brain scientist Geoffrey Raisman spied growth in damaged brain regions of rats through an electron microscope; their brains were forging new connections. This meant brains may change every time a person learns something new.","Of course, that doesn''t mean the brain isn''t affected by the effects of time. Just as height usually declines over the years, so does brain volume: Humans lose about 4 percent every decade starting in their 40s. But that reduction doesn''t necessarily make people think slower; as long as we are alive and functioning, we can alter our brains with new information and experiences.","In fact, scientists now suspect accumulating novel experiences, facts, and skills can keep people''s minds more flexible. New pathways can strengthen our ever-changing mental structure, even as the brain shrinks.","Conventional fixes like word puzzles and brain-training apps can contribute to mental durability. Even something as simple as taking a different route to the grocery store or going somewhere new on vacation can keep the brain healthy.","A desire for new life challenges can further boost brainpower. Research about aging adults who take on new enterprises shows improved function and memory as well as a reduced risk of mental disease. Openness— a characteristic defined by curiosity and a desire for knowledge—may also help folks pass brain tests. Some folks are born with this take-in-the-world atitude, but those who aren''t as genetically gifted aren''t necessarily out of luck. While genes can encourage an interest in doing new things, a 2012 study in the journal Psychology and Aging found completing reasoning tasks like puzzles and number games can enhance that desire for novel experiences, which can, in turn, refresh the brain. That''s why brain scientist Richard Kennedy says “It''s not that old dogs can''t learn new tricks. It''s that maybe old dogs don''t realize why they should.”"]','["Some people have said aging is more a slide into forgetfulness than a journey towards wisdom. However, a growing body of research suggests that late-in-life learning is possible. In reality, education does an aging brain good.","Throughout life, people''s brains constantly renovate themselves. In the late 1960s, British brain scientist Geoffrey Raisman spied growth in damaged brain regions of rats through an electron microscope; their brains were forging new connections. This meant brains may change every time a person learns something new.","Of course, that doesn''t mean the brain isn''t affected by the effects of time. Just as height usually declines over the years, so does brain volume: Humans lose about 4 percent every decade starting in their 40s. But that reduction doesn''t necessarily make people think slower; as long as we are alive and functioning, we can alter our brains with new information and experiences.","In fact, scientists now suspect accumulating novel experiences, facts, and skills can keep people''s minds more flexible. New pathways can strengthen our ever-changing mental structure, even as the brain shrinks.","Conventional fixes like word puzzles and brain-training apps can contribute to mental durability. Even something as simple as taking a different route to the grocery store or going somewhere new on vacation can keep the brain healthy.","A desire for new life challenges can further boost brainpower. Research about aging adults who take on new enterprises shows improved function and memory as well as a reduced risk of mental disease. Openness— a characteristic defined by curiosity and a desire for knowledge—may also help folks pass brain tests. Some folks are born with this take-in-the-world atitude, but those who aren''t as genetically gifted aren''t necessarily out of luck. While genes can encourage an interest in doing new things, a 2012 study in the journal Psychology and Aging found completing reasoning tasks like puzzles and number games can enhance that desire for novel experiences, which can, in turn, refresh the brain. That''s why brain scientist Richard Kennedy says “It''s not that old dogs can''t learn new tricks. It''s that maybe old dogs don''t realize why they should.”"]') ON CONFLICT (id) DO UPDATE SET position=EXCLUDED.position,kind=EXCLUDED.kind,title=EXCLUDED.title,instructions=EXCLUDED.instructions,paragraphs_json=EXCLUDED.paragraphs_json,study_paragraphs_json=EXCLUDED.study_paragraphs_json;
INSERT INTO questions (id,section_id,position,type,prompt,options_json,answer_text,explanation,points) VALUES ('cet4-2024-06-1-section-5-q-51','cet4-2024-06-1-section-5',0,'choice','51. What do some people think of aging adults?','[{"key":"A","text":"Their wisdom grows as time goes by."},{"key":"B","text":"Their memory gradually deteriorates"},{"key":"C","text":"They can benefit from late-in-life learning."},{"key":"D","text":"They are likely to have mental health issues."}]','B','参考答案 B，依据原文整理。首段介绍一种看法：衰老更像滑向遗忘，而非走向智慧，即记忆逐渐退化。',2) ON CONFLICT (id) DO UPDATE SET position=EXCLUDED.position,type=EXCLUDED.type,prompt=EXCLUDED.prompt,options_json=EXCLUDED.options_json,answer_text=EXCLUDED.answer_text,explanation=EXCLUDED.explanation,points=EXCLUDED.points;
INSERT INTO questions (id,section_id,position,type,prompt,options_json,answer_text,explanation,points) VALUES ('cet4-2024-06-1-section-5-q-52','cet4-2024-06-1-section-5',1,'choice','52. What can we conclude from Geoffrey Raisman''s finding?','[{"key":"A","text":"Brain damage seriously hinders one''s learning."},{"key":"B","text":"Brain power weakens slower than we imagine"},{"key":"C","text":"Brains can refresh and improve with learning."},{"key":"D","text":"Brains forge connections under new conditions"}]','C','参考答案 C，依据原文整理。第二段中 Raisman 观察到受损脑区形成新连接，说明学习新事物时大脑可以改变和更新。',2) ON CONFLICT (id) DO UPDATE SET position=EXCLUDED.position,type=EXCLUDED.type,prompt=EXCLUDED.prompt,options_json=EXCLUDED.options_json,answer_text=EXCLUDED.answer_text,explanation=EXCLUDED.explanation,points=EXCLUDED.points;
INSERT INTO questions (id,section_id,position,type,prompt,options_json,answer_text,explanation,points) VALUES ('cet4-2024-06-1-section-5-q-53','cet4-2024-06-1-section-5',2,'choice','53. What is one thing that helps maintain the health of our brain even as it shrinks?','[{"key":"A","text":"Doing daily routines by conventional means."},{"key":"B","text":"Avoiding worrying about our mental durability."},{"key":"C","text":"Imitating old dogs'' way of learning new tricks"},{"key":"D","text":"Approaching everyday tasks in novel ways."}]','D','参考答案 D，依据原文整理。第四、五段说新体验和新路径可保持脑部健康，例如换一条购物路线或去新的度假地点。',2) ON CONFLICT (id) DO UPDATE SET position=EXCLUDED.position,type=EXCLUDED.type,prompt=EXCLUDED.prompt,options_json=EXCLUDED.options_json,answer_text=EXCLUDED.answer_text,explanation=EXCLUDED.explanation,points=EXCLUDED.points;
INSERT INTO questions (id,section_id,position,type,prompt,options_json,answer_text,explanation,points) VALUES ('cet4-2024-06-1-section-5-q-54','cet4-2024-06-1-section-5',3,'choice','54. What does the author say can contribute to the improvement of brain function?','[{"key":"A","text":"Being curious and desiring knowledge."},{"key":"B","text":"Being eager to pass brain tests at an old age."},{"key":"C","text":"Rising to life''s challenges and avoiding risks."},{"key":"D","text":"Boosting immunity to serious mental diseases"}]','A','参考答案 A，依据原文整理。最后一段把 openness 定义为好奇和求知欲，并指出这种特质有助于认知表现。',2) ON CONFLICT (id) DO UPDATE SET position=EXCLUDED.position,type=EXCLUDED.type,prompt=EXCLUDED.prompt,options_json=EXCLUDED.options_json,answer_text=EXCLUDED.answer_text,explanation=EXCLUDED.explanation,points=EXCLUDED.points;
INSERT INTO questions (id,section_id,position,type,prompt,options_json,answer_text,explanation,points) VALUES ('cet4-2024-06-1-section-5-q-55','cet4-2024-06-1-section-5',4,'choice','55. What is the finding of the 2012 study in the journal Psychology and Aging?','[{"key":"A","text":"Wishing to solve puzzles enhances one''s reasoning power."},{"key":"B","text":"Playing number games unexpectedly stimulates one''s memory."},{"key":"C","text":"Desiring new experiences can help to renovate the brain."},{"key":"D","text":"Learning new tricks should not be confined to old dogs only."}]','C','参考答案 C，依据原文整理。2012 年研究发现推理练习能增强对新体验的渴望，而这种渴望又能更新大脑；选项 C 对应后一个发现。',2) ON CONFLICT (id) DO UPDATE SET position=EXCLUDED.position,type=EXCLUDED.type,prompt=EXCLUDED.prompt,options_json=EXCLUDED.options_json,answer_text=EXCLUDED.answer_text,explanation=EXCLUDED.explanation,points=EXCLUDED.points;
